    'GET reads and should not change anything. POST creates something (or triggers an action). PUT replaces a whole resource; PATCH changes part of one; DELETE removes one. Safe methods (GET) can be retried and cached; unsafe ones should not be. Choosing correctly makes APIs predictable and prevents duplicate orders.',
    'Read the label, add a new file, replace a file, correct one line, or shred a file.',
